        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: street-style fit check\nTopic: music production\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 8s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_ZEM41A45GYMY2W6PKH3J6TN8F1",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_SFKQJVGZDD5P0NN83T1TJS6Z6Y",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_331K1X0QSK0KRMZPECXYBFRN4J",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.97,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a street-style fit check about music production for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the street-style fit check \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a slow dolly-in that closes about a third of the distance on an 85mm short telephoto, framing with a tight crop that breaks the subject at the frame edge.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with split gel lighting, teal on the shadow side and magenta on the key side; grade as a bleach-bypass look with crushed saturation and lifted contrast. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Output exactly one prompt paragraph and nothing else \u2014 no labels, no lists, no explanation of your reasoning."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_F724NS72GAQG8N795D53AB31ER",
        "kind": "image-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 700
